    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="1279" n="1267" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg1267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.4016/8–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Poland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-11T14:00:00+02:00">August 11, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 14—1:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. I communicated orally to Minister Foreign Affairs<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d602-f1"/> August 10 contents Department’s telegram 4, July
                        31,<anchor n="69" xml:id="d602-f2"/> received August 8. Rzymowski said both
                    Soviet and British representatives had already made <pb facs="1280" n="1268"
                        xml:id="pg1268"/> similar request with which Polish Government would comply.
                    He made no reservations such as British Chargé had reported (my telegram
                        15<anchor n="71" xml:id="d602-f3"/>).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d602-f1" n="68" xml:id="d602-f1-content">
                <p>Wincenty Rzymowski, Minister of Foreign Affairs in the Polish Provisional
                    Government of National Unity.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d602-f2" n="69" xml:id="d602-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 59, <ref target="#pg1265">p. 1265</ref>.</p>
